@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Hosted same-origin application: one durable application host
node "User's device" <<device>> {
  node "Browser" as Browser <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "Built React frontend\nprivate drafts in memory" as React
    artifact "Browser speech APIs\nopt-in dictation / read-aloud" as Speech
  }
}
node "Public HTTPS reverse proxy" as Proxy <<executionEnvironment>>
node "Durable application host\nrestricted service account" <<device>> {
  node "Python / FastAPI + Uvicorn\nloopback or firewalled private interface" as Backend <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "Backend + compiler" as Python
    artifact "frontend/dist\nserved by FastAPI" as WebAssets
    artifact "Server-only configuration\nSMTP / Google / Gemini credentials" as Secret
  }
  node "Persistent private disk" <<device>> {
    artifact "auth.sqlite3\nidentity / sessions / quotas" as Accounts
    artifact "workspaces/<account UUID>/workspace.sqlite3" as Workspace
    artifact "dictionary/camfranglais.md\n+ extra_lexicon.md (versioned)" as References
    artifact "Per-account audio / generated filenames" as Audio
    artifact "Per-account verified backup ZIPs" as Backups
  }
}
node "Protected off-host backup location" as Recovery <<external storage>>
node "Microphone / speakers" as Devices <<device>>
node "Gemini API" as Gemini <<external service>>
node "Google OAuth + signing keys" as Google <<external service>>
node "SMTP provider" as Mail <<external service>>
node "Browser-selected speech provider\nimplementation-dependent" as SpeechProvider <<external service>>
Browser -- Proxy : HTTPS: frontend + API
Proxy -- Backend : trusted forwarded headers;\nall paths, restricted HTTP
Python ..> Accounts : SQLite transactions
Python ..> Workspace : account-selected transactions + locks
Python ..> Audio : private media I/O
Python ..> Backups : validated snapshots / restore
Python ..> References : read-only lookup
Backend -- Recovery : operator-managed consistent backup
Browser -- Devices : browser permissions
Backend -- Gemini : HTTPS; explicit AI requests
Browser -- Google : HTTPS; optional human authorization
Backend -- Google : HTTPS; code exchange and JWT validation
Backend -- Mail : SMTP STARTTLS; account links
Browser -- SpeechProvider : may use online speech
Secret ..> Python
legend bottom
  Authentication is mandatory for private APIs. CORS is not access control.
  Local pre-hosting testing: browser -> loopback FastAPI, no public proxy required.
  Vite is an optional development server, not the production static host.
  Legacy desktop CSV/audio/profile are separate and never adopted by a hosted account.
  Disk backup requires identity data too; workspace ZIPs alone cannot recover accounts.
  Single durable host only: no ephemeral disk or implied multi-host database cluster.
endlegend
@enduml
